<title>USA: San Francisco library plan to slash staff - report.</title>
<headline>San Francisco library plan to slash staff - report.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Francisco's chief librarian plans to cut $1.2 million from the library's $35 million annual budget through layoffs and reductions in working hours, San Francisco Chronicle reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Chief Librarian Kenneth Dowlin's proposal would eliminate the equivalent of about 93 full-time positions out of a staff of some 900 employees.</p>
<p>The cuts were necessitated by the system's recent financial troubles, which drew fire from Mayor Willie Brown and other San Francisco officials.</p>
<p>Dowlin was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
